This directory contains accounts for testing.
The password that unlocks them is "foobar".

The "good" key files which are supposed to be loadable are ML-DSA-44 key
files ("scheme":1) of the seed of 32 bytes of one value:

- File: UTC--2026-10-21T09-00-00.000000000Z--<address>
  Seed: 32 bytes of 0x0a
- File: aaa
  Seed: 32 bytes of 0x0b
- File: zzz
  Seed: 32 bytes of 0x0c

The other files (including this README) are broken or refused in various ways
and should not be picked up by package accounts:

- File: no-address (missing address field, otherwise same as "aaa")
- File: no-scheme (missing scheme field, otherwise same as "aaa")
- File: other-scheme (scheme field 2, otherwise same as "aaa")
- File: zero (zero address, otherwise same as "aaa")
- File: ecdsa (a secp256k1 key file without scheme field, address
  0xf466859ead1932d743d622cb74fc058882e8648a)
- File: garbage (file with random data)
- File: empty (file with no content)
- File: swapfile~ (should be skipped)
- File: .hiddenfile (should be skipped)
- File: foo/... (should be skipped because it is a directory)
